(5. The frontend calls `/auth/me` to detect the authenticated user.) Tj
T*
(6. If authenticated, the dashboard and email form are displayed.) Tj
T*
(7. The user composes an email, and the app sends it to the backend via `/api/send-email`.) Tj
T*
(8. The backend uses the authenticated user session to send Gmail messages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Notes for interview) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- I maintained functionality while upgrading the UI, focusing on both appearance and) Tj
T*
(usability.) Tj
T*
(- The login flow was made reliable for GitHub Pages by hardcoding the Render API endpoint) Tj
T*
(and using `withCredentials`.) Tj
T*
(- I simplified the app structure by removing unused starter files and using a centralized) Tj
T*
(API utility.) Tj
T*
(- I also added auth session handling and CORS improvements in the backend to support) Tj
T*
(deployed frontend requests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
